Initial startup observation: graphify.exe extract --help failed without output while
Windows showed a python.exe memory-read error. No matching accessible event/WER record.
Plain module --help succeeded, but the initial claim that module invocation alone avoids
the crash was incorrect: the command-specific startup path differs, and a later compound
PowerShell command hid the Python exit. The diagnosis below supersedes that interpretation.
The retained graph hash was rechecked and unchanged after the failed help invocation.

Follow-up crash diagnosis (same session, after a second screenshot): the module entry
point ALSO crashes for extract --help when PYTHONHASHSEED is absent. A faulthandler
probe captured native exit -1073741819 / access violation at os.execvpe, called by
graphify.__main__._pin_hash_seed_if_needed (installed 0.9.67, lines 531/545).
Plain isolated Python startup exits 0. Exact same Graphify help command with only
PYTHONHASHSEED=0 added before startup exits 0 and prints help. This bypasses the proven
crashing self-reexec path; the interpreter/DLL cause underneath it is not established.
The full extraction already used PYTHONHASHSEED=0. No Python reinstall or persistent
machine setting changed. Error dialogs were disabled only in the diagnostic process
and its children, with the parent's previous process-local mode restored afterwards.

Intermediate CLI batch: 12/12 chunks, exit 0, 1089 nodes / 2144 edges written. NOT accepted:
the CLI explicitly reported HANDOFF.md semantic shrink 13 -> 5 despite exit 0.
The pre-batch 833-node graph remains backed up; at that point only HANDOFF needed retry.

Known extraction caveat: the CLI discarded out-of-scope references and reported
